With `--member-invariants`, the member-invariant extension check now covers the
proof hints (statements inside expressions) of the functions in an invariant's
cone, and the lemmas they call, whether or not the cone has a lemma binding.
In them it rejects raw tests and conversions, unbounded choices and quantifiers
over a type that depends on the invariant's type, reads of a field or array
element of such a type (in any expression of the cone, too), and calls of
dynamically bound lemmas. Without this, a hint could assume the type's
invariants while proving a function's postcondition, termination or a callee's
precondition, and prove `false`. The hidden
`--legacy-unchecked-member-invariant-proofs` option restores the former, unsound
check, for migration and comparison only.
